{
  "an8.46:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 8.46 ",
  "an8.46:0.2": "5. Sabbath ",
  "an8.46:0.3": "Anuruddha and the Agreeable Deities ",
  "an8.46:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Kosambī in Ghosita’s monastery. ",
  "an8.46:1.2": "Now at that time Venerable Anuruddha had gone into retreat for the day’s meditation. ",
  "an8.46:1.3": "Then several deities of the Agreeable Host went up to Venerable Anuruddha, bowed, stood to one side, and said to him: ",
  "an8.46:1.4": "“Honorable Anuruddha, we are the deities called ‘Agreeable’. We wield authority and control over three things. ",
  "an8.46:1.5": "We can turn any color we want on the spot. ",
  "an8.46:1.6": "We can get any voice that we want on the spot. ",
  "an8.46:1.7": "We can get any pleasure that we want on the spot. ",
  "an8.46:1.8": "We are the deities called ‘Agreeable’. We wield authority and control over these three things.” ",
  "an8.46:2.1": "Then Venerable Anuruddha thought, ",
  "an8.46:2.2": "“If only these deities would all turn blue, of blue color, clad in blue, adorned with blue!” ",
  "an8.46:2.3": "Then those deities, knowing Anuruddha’s thought, all turned blue. ",
  "an8.46:3.1": "Then Venerable Anuruddha thought, ",
  "an8.46:3.2": "“If only these deities would all turn yellow …” ",
  "an8.46:3.3": "“If only these gods would all turn red …” ",
  "an8.46:3.4": "“If only these gods would all turn white …” ",
  "an8.46:3.5": "Then those deities, knowing Anuruddha’s thought, all turned